    "title": "WrestleMania 42: Bianca Belair returns with surprise announcement about her WWE future",
    "text": "The last time Bianca Belair wrestled was a full year ago at last year's WrestleMania in an instant classic. On Night 1 of WrestleMania 42 in Allegiant Stadium in Las Vegas, however, she made a surprise return to announce her pregnancy with her husband, fellow WWE star Montez Ford.Belair's reveal came directly after Liv Morgan's Women's World Championship win over Stephanie Vaquer, right before the evening's main event match. WrestleMania 42 host and WWE legend John Cena took to the ring to announce the show's attendance at 50,816. He was then met by Belair, who has been absent from WWE programming since suffering a nasty finger injury in her WrestleMania 41 match last April against Iyo Sky and Rhea Ripley.Belair quickly corrected Cena, stating that there was a mistake in the attendance count.Advertisement\"Add one more,\" she said, before revealing her baby bump and noting that she'll remain sidelined for the foreseeable future.The 37-year-old Belair has been a major player atop WWE's women's roster since she arrived and rose through NXT from 2016 to 2020. Belair quickly entered the world title scene and has won WWE's top title three times, along with two Women's Tag Team Championship title reigns alongside Naomi and current WWE Women's Champion Jade Cargill.More from UncrownedCheck out full WrestleMania 42 Night 1 results, highlights and match-by-match updates here.",
